{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-virtual"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter is a wrapper around the core virtual logic."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createvirtualizer","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createVirtualizer"}]},{"type":"code","value":"\nprivate virtualizerController = new VirtualizerController<TScrollElement, TItemElement = unknown>(\n    options: PartialKeys< VirtualizerOptions<TScrollElement, TItemElement>,\n    'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This class stands for a standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Virtualizer"},{"type":"text","value":" instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement.\nThis will create a Lit Controller which can be accessed in the element render method."}]},{"type":"code","value":"render() {\n    const virtualizer = this.virtualizerController.getVirtualizer();\n    const virtualItems = virtualizer.getVirtualItems();\n} \n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createwindowvirtualizer","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createWindowVirtualizer"}]},{"type":"code","value":"private windowVirtualizerController = new WindowVirtualizerController<TItemElement = unknown>(\n    options: PartialKeys< VirtualizerOptions<TItemElement>,\n    'getScrollElement' | 'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This class stands of window-based "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Virtualizer"},{"type":"text","value":" instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"createvirtualizer","text":"createVirtualizer","level":2},{"id":"createwindowvirtualizer","text":"createWindowVirtualizer","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `@tanstack/lit-virtual` adapter is a wrapper around the core virtual logic.\n\n## `createVirtualizer`\n\n```tsx\n\nprivate virtualizerController = new VirtualizerController<TScrollElement, TItemElement = unknown>(\n    options: PartialKeys< VirtualizerOptions<TScrollElement, TItemElement>,\n    'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'\n)\n```\n\nThis class stands for a standard `Virtualizer` instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement.\nThis will create a Lit Controller which can be accessed in the element render method.\n\n```tsx\nrender() {\n    const virtualizer = this.virtualizerController.getVirtualizer();\n    const virtualItems = virtualizer.getVirtualItems();\n} \n)\n```\n\n## `createWindowVirtualizer`\n\n```tsx\nprivate windowVirtualizerController = new WindowVirtualizerController<TItemElement = unknown>(\n    options: PartialKeys< VirtualizerOptions<TItemElement>,\n    'getScrollElement' | 'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'\n```\n\nThis class stands of window-based `Virtualizer` instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Lit Virtual\n---\n\nThe `@tanstack/lit-virtual` adapter is a wrapper around the core virtual logic.\n\n## `createVirtualizer`\n\n```tsx\n\nprivate virtualizerController = new VirtualizerController<TScrollElement, TItemElement = unknown>(\n    options: PartialKeys< VirtualizerOptions<TScrollElement, TItemElement>,\n    'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'\n)\n```\n\nThis class stands for a standard `Virtualizer` instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement.\nThis will create a Lit Controller which can be accessed in the element render method.\n\n```tsx\nrender() {\n    const virtualizer = this.virtualizerController.getVirtualizer();\n    const virtualItems = virtualizer.getVirtualItems();\n} \n)\n```\n\n## `createWindowVirtualizer`\n\n```tsx\nprivate windowVirtualizerController = new WindowVirtualizerController<TItemElement = unknown>(\n    options: PartialKeys< VirtualizerOptions<TItemElement>,\n    'getScrollElement' | 'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'\n```\n\nThis class stands of window-based `Virtualizer` instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement.\n"}
